---
title: Lebanese lentil soup
servings: 8
tags: [lebanese, vegan, make-ahead]
cuisine: lebanese
source: Lebanese Lentil Soup (Shorbet Adas) by Mariam Ezzeddine, Cookin' with Mima, https://www.cookinwithmima.com/lebanese-lentil-soup/
---

Rinse the @red lentils{2.5%cup} until the water runs nearly clear.

Put them in a #large pot{} with the @yellow onion{1}(cubed),
@carrot{1}(large, peeled and cubed), @potato{1}(small, peeled and cubed) and
@water{12%cup}.

Boil ~{45%minutes}, or up to an hour, until the lentils have completely
collapsed. Turn off the heat and leave ~{10%minutes}.

Blend until completely smooth, at least a minute on high, then pour back into
the pot.

Stir the @ground cumin{2%tsp}, @black pepper{1%tsp}(finely ground) and
@baharat{1/2%tsp}(Lebanese seven spice, optional) into a splash of water and add
to the soup with the @salt{1%tbsp} and @parsley{2%tbsp}(chopped).

Bring to a boil, then simmer on low ~{12%minutes}, stirring now and then.

Off the heat, stir in the @lemon juice{3/4%cup}(from about 3 lemons). Serve with
@pita bread{}(fried, optional).

> Blend in batches with the lid vented, or use an immersion blender in the pot.
